 # document-backup
 
 Small local library. Run `npm test`.
+
+Documents are loaded from the primary file first. If it cannot be read, parsed,
+or validated, a valid `.bak` file is used without modifying either file. Saving
+rejects a corrupt existing primary rather than silently repairing it. When
+replacing a valid primary, its exact bytes become the backup before the new
+primary is renamed into place. The primary and backup are separate files, so a
+power loss between those operations is not a two-file transaction.
diff --git a/src/documents.mjs b/src/documents.mjs
index 869977c2d66eacd68d6ac6ba17c5380a7b937bae..17d5f3f88e5656b6a174507073f9274ac61c7031 100644
--- a/src/documents.mjs
